  {
   "id": 533627,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In the isosceles triangle shown, find the missing angles.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/9498d6ea8d4d8ad8.png\" alt=\"A triangle with its interior angles marked x, y, and 77 degrees.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In an isosceles triangle, at least two angles have equal measures. You know the angles at the bottom have equal measure.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x = 77^\\circ\"></span></p>\n<p>The sum of the angle measures must be 180°. A right angle measures 90°.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y + 77 + 77 = 180\"></span></td>\n<td>Add.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y + 154 = 180\"></span></td>\n<td>Subtract.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y = 26^\\circ \"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = {77^ \\circ }\">x = {77^ \\circ }</span> and <span data-math=\"y = {26^ \\circ }\">.</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
